WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.640
Hey, folks, welcome to another SCP Explained
community questions episode.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.540
Today, we’re answering all your burning
concerns about the multiverse’s most monstrous

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.519
monarch, the Scarlet King You may remember
the episode where SCP-343 was kind enough

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:18.550
to come chat with us directly about his queries,
but thankfully, the Scarlet King hasn’t

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:20.010
been quite so hands-on—
WRONG!

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:26.300
It is I, puny mortals, your future ruler in
blood, pain, and terror.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:35.870
The howling horror, the Crimson Khan, the
Scarlet King himself.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:42.220
Before I tear down the walls of your universe
and destroy every last one of you, I will

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:47.410
first take the time to address your idiotic
questions, so that your hope may be thoroughly

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:52.140
crushed before I crush your world to match!

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:56.770
The small-minded Pandaua said, “Question:
Even though you have taken out literally God's

00:00:56.770 --> 00:01:09.030
from your universe and you ruled some of them,
how do you feel to know that you have new

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:16.170
gods to prey and possibly worry about in the
SCP foundation?”

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:17.570
Ha!

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:26.480
Do you think your worthless gods hold any
surprises for me?

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:32.140
I was slaughtering gods by the millions before
your universe’s inception.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:41.159
By the time your worthless forbearers were
slithering from the primordial soup, I had

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:49.320
conquered and subjugated greater pantheons
of outer-gods than your minds can even conceive.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.740
The Scarlet King worries about nothing!

00:01:53.740 --> 00:02:08.200
The worthless Ricardo Anguiano said, “Question:
What do you think about the other anomalous

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:30.350
GOI such as the Serpent's hand or the Chaos
Insurgency What does the boot think of ants

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.990
it’s crushing?

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:39.010
Those pathetic bookworms are acolytes of knowledge
that will become meaningless under my rule.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:44.980
I will incinerate the Library and toast skewered
Serpents on its heat.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:48.069
And this so-called Chaos Insurgency?

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:50.540
Don’t make me laugh.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:58.569
They wouldn’t know true Chaos if it tore
their world asunder beneath them.

00:02:58.569 --> 00:03:04.130
The feeble Tblaster said, “Ah yes, Mr.King
is it?

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:17.090
I have but a simple question, what other SCP's
do you enjoy, and if you had to name another

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:24.680
SCP as a close friend, who (or what) would
that be?”

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:25.680
Enjoy?

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:33.319
The only things I “Enjoy” are pain, suffering,
subjugation, and desolation.

00:03:33.319 --> 00:03:45.349
I suppose the ones I despise the least, comparatively,
are those that seek to further my own goals

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:54.349
of returning the universe back to its true
state of primal violence.

00:03:54.349 --> 00:03:57.580
I’ll destroy them last.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:06.310
The quivering Jet Ender said, “I would keep
it simple but useful: Can 682 be destroyed

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.310
permanently?

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:14.290
Not necessarily any information about how,
just getting the answer directly from 682's

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:22.009
supposed father of whether it's even worth
the trouble to keep trying to terminate that

00:04:22.009 --> 00:04:23.009
dang lizard.”

00:04:23.009 --> 00:04:24.309
The only thing that can destroy anything and
everything is me.

00:04:24.309 --> 00:04:25.479
No exceptions.

00:04:25.479 --> 00:04:31.909
But I wouldn’t destroy Atanti-ql-Paneu until
he has outlived his usefulness.

00:04:31.909 --> 00:04:47.099
Everything will end, but it will only end
when I see fit.

00:04:47.099 --> 00:04:53.949
Speaking of which...

00:04:53.949 --> 00:05:04.289
The inadequate Aeris Skyla said, “Question:
If you hate all of existence so much, Why

00:05:04.289 --> 00:05:08.330
not get rid of your children?

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:13.029
Like, they’re technically Part OF Existence.

00:05:13.029 --> 00:05:19.569
so How come you hate Existence, but Make Existence
(Your Children)?”

00:05:19.569 --> 00:05:21.789
I don’t like repeating myself, human!

00:05:21.789 --> 00:05:25.349
As I said before, everything has its time.

00:05:25.349 --> 00:05:32.460
For the time being, my daughters are still
of use to me.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:42.569
I will not destroy them until they have played
their part in my crimson crusade.

00:05:42.569 --> 00:05:45.240
Next question!

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:55.169
The unspeakably weak Ross Albatross said,
“I'd present them with a query: "Have you

00:05:55.169 --> 00:06:00.470
ever considered wearing something other than
red?

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:10.969
With the dark colored horns on top, you're
definitely more of a winter than a summer.

00:06:10.969 --> 00:06:28.460
Also if your skin is inflamed with rosacea
I have a really good serum for that" Next

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:40.159
thing you know the scarlet king changes his
name to gold king and forces everyone in the

00:06:40.159 --> 00:06:48.839
world to wear only complimentary colors that
fit their own complexion and hair color.”

00:06:48.839 --> 00:06:57.289
My armor will be another color than red when
you learn to bleed rainbows.

00:06:57.289 --> 00:07:08.360
I will not be changing my name again - I’ve
done that enough for one eternal lifetime

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:17.349
already - Harak, Khnith-hgor, Shormaush Urdal
- and the Scarlet King seems to have stuck.

00:07:17.349 --> 00:07:26.309
The moronic Xavier Valencia said, “Question:
When did this hatred for existence begin,

00:07:26.309 --> 00:07:39.379
like did something happen to you or have you
always had it?”

00:07:39.379 --> 00:07:43.279
My hatred for existence began when I began
to exist.

00:07:43.279 --> 00:07:46.500
What a sick joke all of this is.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:56.349
We only live to die, regardless of the blink
of existence in between.

00:07:56.349 --> 00:08:07.909
I’m merely hurrying a natural process along
to its logical conclusion.

00:08:07.909 --> 00:08:17.740
The blithering Mister_Muffin said, “I would
just ask him, how his day's been, if he is

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:28.189
going through something and needs someone
to lighten his mood, you know, the usual.”

00:08:28.189 --> 00:08:36.460
Killing you and your entire family horribly
would lighten my mood, Muffin Man.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:43.710
Any pathetic attempts to console me will only
increase my rage.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:54.310
The insolent Adam Arfaq said, “I have a
question : How come you couldn't get to earth

00:08:54.310 --> 00:09:06.580
when you destroyed powerful gods and big planets
without even having to use your full power.”

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:08.040
You dare question my power, Arfaq?

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:14.970
Being shut out of your worthless dimension
is only a temporary affliction.

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:23.210
Before you know it, the walls that keep you
safe will crack and crumble.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:31.990
The last thing you will ever see is my dread
armies blotting out the sky, ready to tear

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:36.280
every last one of you to shreds.

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:41.620
Then you will know my true power.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:51.860
A buffoon known as TheSauce said, “I would
simply ask him the question everyone has on

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:59.520
their mind, "How much wood would a woodchuck
chuck if a woodchuck could chuck wood?" and

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:02.460
I await his answer.”

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:09.080
This was a terrible question, and I hate you.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:20.840
When a Scarlet sun rises over your world,
I will ensure that your death is especially

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:23.040
painful for this.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:34.520
An insect named Denzell Brown said, “The
first question you usually have to ask a being

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:43.270
like this is, "In your rampage across the
multiverse, have you ever encountered another

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:53.910
version of yourself or one comparable in terms
of power or presence?

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:54.910
If so, what happened?

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:56.970
Can more than one version of you exist in
the same space?”

00:10:56.970 --> 00:11:01.730
There is only one Scarlet King.

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:08.450
I am an immutable being, a fixed point.

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:17.940
I have never had an equal in all the desolate
plains of the universes I’ve rendered into

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:18.940
atomic fragments.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:22.370
This is my power, this is my unity.

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:28.860
I will bring the multiverse together in the
quiet rift of oblivion.

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:30.210
Next question!

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:42.130
A worm named Riftz said, “I would ask him:
WHO do you consider the greatest threat to

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.410
your goal?”

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:55.710
There ARE no threats to my goal, only bumps
in the road.

00:11:55.710 --> 00:12:07.650
There is no threat, there is nothing that
will stop me from fulfilling my destiny.

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:11.630
Hey, get out of here!

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:13.220
Next question!

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:14.810
NEXT QUESTION!

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:24.910
The misguided Archbishop said, “Question:
Have you ever faced a foe that's given you

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:27.180
a good challenge.

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:34.000
If so, how did you manage to beat them?”

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:47.500
Many of the Gods I once faced when I was a
weaker being gave me the closest battles I’ve

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:50.850
had in trillions of years.

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:59.570
Thankfully, after defeating them, I feasted
on their flesh, making me even stronger.

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:10.300
A weakling named Neight Fiend said, “Question:
Do you meet with Bright for poker every Tuesday

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:11.300
or Wednesday?

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:19.280
Cause let’s face it, dude has to be one
of your best friends, or your worst enemies.”

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:28.740
You are a fool if you think a mere human could
ever be on my level, with or without some

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:33.860
garish piece of magical jewelry.

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:40.400
In his last moments, this Dr. Bright will
thank me, as I rip that medallion from his

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:43.670
stolen neck and crush it in my fist.

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:47.750
A peasant named Static Production said, “I
will ask him.

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:50.650
What does he gain out of destroying the earth?

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:54.529
Is it really his goal or is he trying to impress
someone.

00:13:54.529 --> 00:13:58.550
I would also ask does he like pineapple on
pizza?”

00:13:58.550 --> 00:13:59.550
I will gain peace.

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:00.550
Silence.

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:01.550
Blessed emptiness.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:09.810
In the destruction of all things, I will look
across a quiet multiverse and breathe a sigh

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:11.600
of immense relief.

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:16.100
And my favorite pizza topping is fallen warriors,
sliced very thin.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:21.090
The mindless W1ND General said, “I'd ask
him if he knows anything about other multiverses

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:36.430
aside from the SCP multiverse, like star wars,
lord of the rings, halo, h.p lovecraft, creepypasta,

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:43.750
etc, if he does, what does he know about them?”

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:50.690
I have been there and destroyed them all already.

00:14:50.690 --> 00:15:00.300
Darth Vader
, I felled in a single blow as he begged for

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.300
mercy.

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:07.360
Gandalf I burned until not even ashes remained.

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:15.980
The so-called “Master Chief” , I cast
into an endless black hole.

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:20.820
Azathoth was torn apart by my minions.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:26.310
I personally killed Jeff the Killer . You
will be next, earthling.

00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:28.300
You will be next.

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:31.790
Supreme Spider - Who are we kidding here?

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:39.670
Only I am truly Supreme - said, “I would
ask him: if in a hypothetical situation he

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:50.970
managed to reach his goal of annihilating
everything, what would he do after?”

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:51.970
Laugh.

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:52.970
Next question!

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:57.410
The platitudinous Mes de cent said, “Question:
What is existing for you in particular?

00:15:57.410 --> 00:16:02.470
Do you have a body capable of feeling things
like touch or smell, are you just a conscience

00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:08.540
capable to be manifested, or something so
alien that can't be explained with our language?”

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:13.340
I am able to exist as a fixed point in timespace
while also operating as a diffuse consciousness

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:21.210
across the scope of the multiverse, existing
at varying degrees of strength and influence

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:26.000
depending on the operations of my acolytes.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:35.010
On earth, I can only sense feelings and impressions
until the gate is opened.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:39.690
And rest assured, it WILL be opened for me.

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:46.060
The machine-loving Brolylomaniac said, “What
are your thoughts on Yaldabaoth and Mekhane?

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:55.910
Considering they created what one of the things
you hate the most I am quite curious about

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:58.700
your thoughts on them.”

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:02.880
Mere pretenders to the Scarlet Throne.

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:18.299
Their petty squabbles over the fate of something
as inconsequential as the human race is simply

00:17:18.299 --> 00:17:19.409
embarrassing.

00:17:19.409 --> 00:17:30.600
If Mekhane thinks he’s the “Broken God”
now, oh, just wait until I get my claws on

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:31.600
him.

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:40.889
A nerd named Dr. Veronica said, “If you
were forced to fight King Crimson from Jojo's

00:17:40.889 --> 00:17:45.200
Bizarre Adventure , who would win in that
battle between King Crimson vs Crimson King?

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:49.049
Diavolo says that he's the king of kings,
after all, so the two of you would seemingly

00:17:49.049 --> 00:17:50.049
be mortal enemies.”

00:17:50.049 --> 00:17:54.909
This means nothing to me.

00:17:54.909 --> 00:18:02.070
You should spend less time reading your picture
books and more time preparing for me to breach

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:03.399
your dimension and destroy all of you!

00:18:03.399 --> 00:18:06.279
A foolhardy mortal named Green said, “Question:
How do you feel about being looked down upon

00:18:06.279 --> 00:18:07.740
as an ant?”

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:09.950
I wouldn’t know.

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:13.619
It’s never happened to me.

00:18:13.619 --> 00:18:18.759
How does it make you feel, insect?

00:18:18.759 --> 00:18:25.200
A bootlicker named James Rodgers said, “I
would ask him if he was hiring.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:33.950
Since I know every single scp and everything
about the 05 Council I'm sure I could be of

00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:34.950
assistance to him.”

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:35.950
You can assist me in sabotaging the works
of the SCP Foundation, who are slightly more

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:36.950
irritating than your average humans.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:37.950
They have gained an awareness of me and my
plans, and thus, they must be eliminated in

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:39.740
order to prevent any barriers to my plans.

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:46.169
In exchange for your loyalty, I’ll kill
you quickly and personally, and you will have

00:18:46.169 --> 00:18:47.830
the honor of dying at my hands.

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:50.940
The meaningless collection of letters MTTNYN
said, “Question: What is your favorite beverage

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:54.970
to enjoy after a day of destruction and mayhem?”

00:18:54.970 --> 00:18:58.799
The blood and tears of my enemies!

00:18:58.799 --> 00:19:00.660
Next question!

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:09.850
The appropriately named Pig Master said, “I'd
ask him "what's the deal with airline food?”

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:12.860
Humans survive for an incredibly brief period
of time.

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:16.499
Every time I blink, another several thousand
of you will fizzle out of existence, soon

00:19:16.499 --> 00:19:20.350
to be forgotten, another faceless soul in
the great churn.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:32.679
None of you will live long enough to have
any meaningful impact on your world, other

00:19:32.679 --> 00:19:35.570
than sucking up resources and creating a mess.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:41.379
In your final years, unless you die young
or violently, you will feel your body and

00:19:41.379 --> 00:19:43.119
mind starting to fail.

00:19:43.119 --> 00:19:45.490
Little by little, your faculties will leave
you.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:46.490
You will break down.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:53.629
You will exit this world just as afraid and
feeble and infantile as you entered it, and

00:19:53.629 --> 00:19:57.960
after it, an eternity of nothing awaits.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:07.790
So you distract yourself from this immutable
and inevitable reality by instead focusing

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:14.330
on details as trivial as the poor taste of
food on planes.

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:21.000
The gutless Jason Gutmann said, “I would
ask him if he reads high fantasy and science

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:24.879
fiction to get inspiration for his conquests.”

00:20:24.879 --> 00:20:25.879
No!

00:20:25.879 --> 00:20:29.110
Authors of your feeble fiction get faint impressions
of my dark conquests in the forms of nightmares

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:30.110
they cannot understand or shake.

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:34.080
When they awaken, they bake these impressions
into their work in hopes of exorcising them.

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:38.919
So your “high fantasy” and “science
fiction” get their inspiration from me,

00:20:38.919 --> 00:20:39.919
not the other way around.

00:20:39.919 --> 00:20:40.919
The blabbering Olivia Nealer said, “Dear
Scarlet King,

00:20:40.919 --> 00:20:42.259
Have you ever considered taking a break from
planning the end of all living beings to try

00:20:42.259 --> 00:20:43.759
and engage in some artistic recreational activities?

00:20:43.759 --> 00:20:45.909
There's colouring-in, painting, pitching a
play, creating sculptures, building Lego,

00:20:45.909 --> 00:20:46.909
and creating film media.

00:20:46.909 --> 00:20:54.190
If you ever considered doing one of these
activities, which would you do?”

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:58.360
Olivia, you misunderstand me, I already have
a number of creative pursuits.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:03.480
I create fear in my countless victims.

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:09.860
I assemble armies from rabbles of sadistic
demons and incomprehensible entities.

00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:10.860
I create dark schemes for the conquest of
the multiverse, each with intricate and masterful

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:11.860
details.

00:21:11.860 --> 00:21:12.860
And if Destruction is also a form of creation,
then nobody is more creative than me.

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:13.940
The disgustingly dull April Mornings said,
“I’ve thought long and hard about this

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:18.529
and what I’d like to ask is as follows;
What kind of feline companion does one have?

00:21:18.529 --> 00:21:22.340
Knowing that all cats are basically bent on
world domination, it behooves oneself to align

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.340
with said company.”

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:25.480
I have no feline companions, and when I enter
your universe, I will destroy you and your

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:26.480
cat.

00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:27.480
Next question!

00:21:27.480 --> 00:21:28.480
The gormless DifferenceYT said, “Question:
How often do you wash your body?”

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:30.440
I wash my body in the blood of my enemies
every time I battle.

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:31.440
Which is extremely often!

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:32.639
The grossly sentimental Joao Garcia said,
“My question would be: "Are you bored?

00:21:32.639 --> 00:21:33.639
Lonely?

00:21:33.639 --> 00:21:34.639
Wanna chat?”

00:21:34.639 --> 00:21:37.190
I can never feel bored when crushing my enemies,
seeing them driven before me, hearing the

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:38.190
lamentations of their women, and them crushing
their women, too.

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:39.190
Being lonely, on the other hand, is my intention.

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:40.190
I despise having to spend time around any
other living beings.

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:41.190
And no, I don’t want to chat.

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:42.940
Platypus King said, “Do you like platypuses?”

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:44.739
All you have ever known will burn, Platypus
King.

00:21:44.739 --> 00:21:45.739
The perverse Coffee Addict said, “My burning
question would have to be: Are you single?

00:21:45.739 --> 00:21:46.739
;)”

00:21:46.739 --> 00:21:47.739
No.

00:21:47.739 --> 00:21:48.739
I did have a wife once, but I crushed her
to death and used her blood to paint my armor.

00:21:48.739 --> 00:21:49.739
Since then, I have taken my seven daughters
as my brides.

00:21:49.739 --> 00:21:50.739
TLC has been in touch about licensing a reality
show.

00:21:50.739 --> 00:21:51.759
I destroyed every representative they sent
to my kingdom.

00:21:51.759 --> 00:21:54.320
The snivveling Emerald Inferno0 said, “I
would ask him if there was a possibility to

00:21:54.320 --> 00:21:56.179
turn me into basically a less powerful but
still pretty powerful version of him.”

00:21:56.179 --> 00:21:57.179
I can turn you into a steaming pile of ash.

00:21:57.179 --> 00:21:58.179
That’s my best offer.

00:21:58.179 --> 00:21:59.179
Crimson Goregutter - Hmm, I quite like that
name - said, “I would ask him why he thinks

00:21:59.179 --> 00:22:00.179
destroying the multiverse would stop the pain
he has suffered because if he does he will

00:22:00.179 --> 00:22:02.730
be completely and truly alone forever suffering
the isolation for all eternity.”

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:03.750
And that is exactly how I like it.

00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:04.750
When I’ve destroyed everything else, in
destroying myself the universe will then finally

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:05.750
be silent.

00:22:05.750 --> 00:22:06.750
But worry not.

00:22:06.750 --> 00:22:07.750
There will be plenty of time for violence,
howling, and bloody conquest before then.

00:22:07.750 --> 00:22:08.750
The hopelessly naive MassTV said, “Has he
ever considered becoming a Super Hero?

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:09.750
Put on a cape or cowl, save people from a
few natural disasters, and get the love &amp; admiration

00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:10.750
of an entire world.”

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:11.750
I have no interest in saving people.

00:22:11.750 --> 00:22:12.750
I don’t want their love and admiration.

00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:13.750
I want their fear, their screams, their blood.

00:22:13.750 --> 00:22:14.750
No hero will save them.

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:15.750
The defeatist Vixenlady said, “I'd tell
him that destroying all human life is the

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:16.750
right thing to do.”

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:17.750
I am glad to hear you approve of my mission.

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:18.750
As a treat, I’ll destroy you first when
I get into your dimension.

00:22:18.750 --> 00:22:19.750
The Scarlet Sayer, “I'd ask him" what are
your thoughts on anime waifus, do demonic

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:20.750
beings appeal to you or are we nothing more
than gross nats trying to present ourselves

00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:21.750
as if we were one like you".”

00:22:21.750 --> 00:22:22.750
You should feel deeply embarrassed for even
asking this, Scarlet Sayer.

00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:23.750
Also, change your name.

00:22:23.750 --> 00:22:24.750
If you infringe on me anymore, you’ll hear
from my bloodthirsty inter-dimensional lawyers.

00:22:24.750 --> 00:22:25.750
And if you think I’m cruel, you have no
idea what they’ll do to you.

00:22:25.750 --> 00:22:26.750
Lonely Guy said, “Have you ever considered
anger management classes?”

00:22:26.750 --> 00:22:27.750
I did join an Anger Management group once,
but I had them all liquidated for being insolent

00:22:27.750 --> 00:22:28.750
in the end.

00:22:28.750 --> 00:22:29.750
The truly infuriating Johnny The Gamer said,
“My question is simple.

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:30.750
Why destroy existence and conquer gods when
you could just binge every conceivable tv

00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:31.750
show or anime ever?

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:32.750
Seeing how you're immortal and such you certainly
have the time.”

00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:33.750
Because having an eternal life is still having
a life, “Johnny.”

00:22:33.750 --> 00:22:34.750
And I have better things to do than waste
my time on binging your worthless television

00:22:34.750 --> 00:22:35.750
shows and anime.

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:36.750
When I eventually destroy you, it will be
a mercy.

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:37.750
...I am looking forward to the last season
of Better Call Saul, though.

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:38.750
The not-at-all-foxy Foxy Tv said, “Everybody
always asks "who's the scarlet King?"

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:39.750
"Whats the Scarlet King" i wanna know...how
is the Scarlet King?”

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:40.750
He’s furious after answering all of these
moronic questions!

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:41.750
My life is eternal and this still felt like
a profound waste of my time.

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:42.750
Everyone who took part in this, I hope you
know, you’re on my list.

00:22:42.750 --> 00:22:43.750
And when my terrible armies breach this dimension,
rest assured, they’ll be coming after you

00:22:43.750 --> 00:22:44.750
first!

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:45.750
Now go check out “Children of SCP-001 The
Scarlet King - Is SCP-999 Really His Son?”

00:22:45.750 --> 00:22:46.750
and “SCP-001 - How Actually Powerful is
the Scarlet King?” for more of the literal

00:22:46.750 --> 00:22:46.755
worst guy in the multiverse!

